                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-12-14"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1896</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 613.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In further reference to your No. 505, of
                    June 2, 1896, and my No. 601 of the 6th ultimo, relative to the case of the
                    brothers Glean, I have the honor to inclose herewith a copy, with translation,
                    of a note received from the Spanish Government in which the grounds for the
                    arrest of said brothers Glean and other considerations upon the same subject are
                    set forth.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>








